{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 7. Networks with incomplete data\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook shows how to use the '--regularized' flag in Infomap. It helps prevent the detection of spurious modules in networks, especially when dealing with incomplete data, such as missing links or inaccurate link weights."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "%matplotlib inline\n",
    "\n",
    "from infomap import Infomap\n",
    "import networkx as nx\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "%reload_ext autoreload\n",
    "%autoreload 2\n",
    "import util"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Here, we use a synthetic network with 100 nodes and an average node degree 14.5. The network has 3 planted modules."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# First, we explore communities that Infomap detects in the network when all links are provided.\n",
    "\n",
    "G = nx.read_edgelist(\"data/VII_network_complete.dat\", nodetype=int)\n",
    "nodesize = {node: 1.4 for node in G.nodes()}\n",
    "pos = nx.spring_layout(G, seed=42)\n",
    "nx.set_node_attributes(G, pos, \"pos\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 800x400 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Infomap detects planted modules accurately. \n",
    "\n",
    "im = Infomap(silent = True, two_level = True, num_trials = 10)\n",
    "im.add_networkx_graph(G)\n",
    "im.run()\n",
    "\n",
    "nodelist = G.nodes\n",
    "modules = dict(im.modules)\n",
    "\n",
    "util.partition(G, initial_partition=modules, no_infomap=True)\n",
    "util.plot_network_regularization(G)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Here, we compare partitions Infomap detects in the network after removing a fraction of links randomly, with and without the flag 'regularized'. We can control the strength of the prior by using 'regularization_strength'. In this small network, we set 'regularization_strength' to 0.7; for larger networks (>300 nodes), we suggest using the default value of 1."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# The network after 50% of the links were removed.\n",
    "\n",
    "G_50 = nx.read_edgelist(\"data/VII_network_incomplete_50.dat\", nodetype=int)\n",
    "nx.set_node_attributes(G_50, pos, \"pos\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 800x400 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# The standard map equation can overfit to the noise and detect small spurious modules.\n",
    "\n",
    "im = Infomap(silent = True, two_level = True, num_trials = 10)\n",
    "im.add_networkx_graph(G_50)\n",
    "im.run()\n",
    "\n",
    "nodelist = G_50.nodes\n",
    "modules = dict(im.modules)\n",
    "\n",
    "util.partition(G_50, initial_partition=modules, no_infomap=True)\n",
    "util.plot_network_regularization(G_50)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 800x400 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# The regularized map equation prevents overfitting and detects planted modules.\n",
    "\n",
    "im = Infomap(silent = True, two_level = True, num_trials = 10, regularized=True, regularization_strength=0.7)\n",
    "im.add_networkx_graph(G_50)\n",
    "im.run()\n",
    "\n",
    "nodelist = G_50.nodes\n",
    "modules_regularized = dict(im.modules)\n",
    "\n",
    "util.partition(G_50, initial_partition=modules_regularized, no_infomap=True)\n",
    "util.plot_network_regularization(G_50)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### In this example, 70% of the links are removed. With only 30% of links left, the network structure doesn't reveal evidence of planted communities."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# The network after 70% of the links were removed.\n",
    "\n",
    "G_30 = nx.read_edgelist(\"data/VII_network_incomplete_30.dat\", nodetype=int)\n",
    "nx.set_node_attributes(G_30, pos, \"pos\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 9,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 800x400 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# The standard map equation overfits to the noise and detects many small spurious modules.\n",
    "\n",
    "im = Infomap(silent = True, two_level = True, num_trials = 10)\n",
    "im.add_networkx_graph(G_30)\n",
    "im.run()\n",
    "\n",
    "nodelist = G_30.nodes\n",
    "modules = dict(im.modules)\n",
    "\n",
    "util.partition(G_30, initial_partition=modules, no_infomap=True)\n",
    "util.plot_network_regularization(G_30)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 800x400 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# The regularized map equation detects no modules if the network structure is too sparse.\n",
    "\n",
    "im = Infomap(silent = True, two_level = True, num_trials = 10, regularized=True, regularization_strength=0.7)\n",
    "im.add_networkx_graph(G_30)\n",
    "im.run()\n",
    "\n",
    "nodelist = G_30.nodes\n",
    "modules_regularized = dict(im.modules)\n",
    "\n",
    "util.partition(G_30, initial_partition=modules_regularized, no_infomap=True)\n",
    "util.plot_network_regularization(G_30)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": []
  }
